---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Legal from '../components/Legal.astro';
import Tbc from '../components/Tbc.astro';

// DRAFT FOR LEGAL REVIEW. Prepared against the Personal Data Protection Act
// 2010 (Act 709). Not legal advice. Must be reviewed by a Malaysian lawyer
// before publication, and re-reviewed if any analytics, advertising pixel or
// booking system is added later.
const title = 'Privacy Policy | Cellove Wellness';
const description =
  'How Cellove Wellness collects, uses and protects personal data, and your rights under the Personal Data Protection Act 2010.';
---
<Page title={title} description={description}>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    heading="Privacy Policy"
    body="What we collect when you contact us, why we hold it, and what you can ask us to do with it."
  />
  <Legal>
    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <strong>Please do not send detailed medical information through this website.</strong>
        Tell us the general area you want help with. Anything clinical is better discussed
        in consultation, where it can be recorded and protected properly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This website is operated by <Tbc what="registered legal name" />, company registration
      number <Tbc what="SSM registration number" />, registered at <Tbc what="registered address" />,
      trading as Cellove Wellness. In this policy, &ldquo;we&rdquo; and &ldquo;us&rdquo; mean that company.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are the data user for the purposes of the Personal Data Protection Act 2010
      (Act 709) of Malaysia, which governs how we handle your personal data.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What this policy covers</h2>
    <p>
      It covers personal data we collect through this website and through enquiries that
      start here. It does not cover the clinical records we keep about patients we treat,
      which are governed separately by Malaysian medical records and confidentiality
      obligations, nor does it cover other companies&rsquo; websites we link to.
    </p>

    <h2>3. What we collect</h2>
    <h3>Information you give us</h3>
    <p>When you use the enquiry form, we collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your name;</li>
      <li>your email address;</li>
      <li>your phone or WhatsApp number, if you choose to give one;</li>
      <li>whatever you write in the message field.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Your name and email are required because we cannot reply without them. Everything
      else is optional. We do not ask for your identity card number, date of birth, home
      address, occupation, income or payment details through this website, and you should
      not send them.
    </p>

    <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
    <p>
      Our hosting provider, <Tbc what="hosting provider" />, keeps standard server logs that
      may include your IP address, browser type and the pages you requested. These are used
      to keep the site running and secure, not to build a profile of you.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>This website sets no cookies and runs no analytics, advertising pixels or
      third-party trackers.</strong> See our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Health information</h2>
    <p>
      Information about your physical or mental health is <strong>sensitive personal
      data</strong> under the Act, and may only be processed with your explicit consent. If
      you choose to describe a health concern in the message field, you are giving us that
      consent for the sole purpose of answering your enquiry.
    </p>
    <p>
      We would rather you did not. The enquiry form is ordinary email infrastructure, not a
      clinical system. Say which area you want to discuss and leave the detail for the
      consultation.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Why we use your data, and on what basis</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>To answer your enquiry</strong> and arrange a consultation if you want one. Basis: your consent, given when you submit the form.</li>
      <li><strong>To keep a record of what was asked and answered</strong>, so that anything we tell you is traceable. Basis: our legitimate interest in running a medical service responsibly.</li>
      <li><strong>To keep the website secure.</strong> Basis: our legitimate interest in preventing abuse.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not use your data for marketing unless you separately ask us to, and we do not
      sell, rent or trade it to anyone.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Who else sees it</h2>
    <p>We share personal data only with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>our hosting provider, <Tbc what="hosting provider" />;</li>
      <li>the service that delivers and stores enquiry submissions, <Tbc what="form processor and where data is stored" />;</li>
      <li>professional advisers, or a regulator or court, where we are legally required to.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Where any of these store data outside Malaysia, we remain responsible for it and
      require them to protect it to the standard the Act expects.
    </p>

    <h2>7. WhatsApp</h2>
    <p>
      The WhatsApp buttons on this site open a conversation in WhatsApp, which is operated by
      Meta, not by us. Once you are in WhatsApp you are subject to Meta&rsquo;s own privacy
      terms, and Meta can see that you contacted us. We control only what happens to the
      messages after we receive them. If you would rather Meta were not involved, email us at
      <Tbc what="general enquiries email" /> instead.
    </p>

    <h2>8. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      Enquiries that do not lead to a consultation are deleted after
      <Tbc what="retention period for enquiries" />. If you become a patient, your clinical
      records are kept for the period Malaysian medical record-keeping requirements set,
      which is longer and sits outside this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the Act you may ask us to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you;</li>
      <li><strong>Correct</strong> it if it is wrong or out of date;</li>
      <li><strong>Withdraw your consent</strong> to us processing it, at any time;</li>
      <li><strong>Limit</strong> how we process it, including telling us to stop contacting you;</li>
      <li><strong>Delete</strong> it, where we are not required to keep it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Write to <Tbc what="data protection contact name" /> at <Tbc what="data protection email" />.
      We will respond within the period the Act allows. There is no charge for a reasonable
      request. If you are not satisfied with our answer, you may complain to the Personal Data
      Protection Commissioner of Malaysia.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Security</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served over HTTPS and access to enquiries is limited to staff who need it.
      No transmission over the internet is completely secure, which is the practical reason
      clinical detail belongs in consultation rather than in a web form.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Children</h2>
    <p>
      This website is not directed at children under 18. If a minor needs care, a parent or
      guardian should make the enquiry.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we change this policy we will update the date at the top. If we ever add analytics,
      advertising or online booking, we will update this policy and ask for your consent
      before any tracking begins.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <Tbc what="data protection contact name" />, <Tbc what="data protection email" />,
      <Tbc what="business phone" />, <Tbc what="registered address" />.
    </p>
  </Legal>
</Page>
